course: dictionary
lesson: 3954
title: Fur and keeping warm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fur is the soft, thick hair that covers the bodies of many animals, like cats, dogs, rabbits and bears. Fur keeps these mammals warm because it traps air close to the skin, and the trapped air stops the cold outside from taking the body's heat away.
explain: Fur can also mean a coat or piece of clothing made from animal fur, like a fur coat. Fake fur is soft material made to look like animal fur, so you can have the look without using a real animal's coat.
explain: Fur can be countable or uncountable, so check the clues. «In 1608 the French founded Québec and traded furs with First Nations» means animal fur made into goods, because furs are things you can trade. «Covered in fur» means the hair on an animal's body.
fact: Fur is the soft, thick hair that covers many mammals, such as cats, dogs, rabbits and bears.
fact: Fur keeps mammals warm by trapping air close to the body.
fact: Animals in cold places often have thick fur, and many grow thicker fur in winter and shed it in spring.
fact: «Fox droppings often hold fur and seeds», so rangers can learn which animals live in a place by studying them.
fact: «Burdock burrs hook onto fur», so seeds can travel far away from their parent plant.
exercise: In «covered in fur», what does fur mean? | *Soft thick hair that covers an animal's body | A coat made from metal | A type of plant seed | A kind of cold weather
exercise: Why do many animals in cold places have thick fur? | To make them run faster | To help them sleep | To hide their food | *To keep them warm by trapping air
exercise: Which animal's droppings often hold fur and seeds? | Rabbit | Deer | *Fox | Bird
test: What does «fake fur» mean? | *Soft material made to look like animal fur | A cold, wet day | Real fur taken from a wild animal | A kind of seed
test: Which of these animals has fur on its body? | Snail | Lizard | *Rabbit | Fish
exam: In «even pollen licked off their fur can damage the kidneys», what is fur? | A kind of leaf | Fake fur from a shop | *The soft hair covering a cat's body | A coat made from animal fur
